# ====================
# Documentation (Internal)
# ====================
# Note: `docs/*` (not `docs/`) so git still descends into the directory and the
# negation below can take effect. A directory excluded outright is never walked,
# and any `!` rule for a path inside it is silently ignored.
docs/*
DEVELOPER_GUIDE.md
JOBS_DATASET_SPEC.md
PASS3_PROMPT.md
CONTRIBUTING.md

# Architecture Decision Records are public — they are the record of why the
# system is shaped the way it is, and must survive the blanket docs/ ignore.
!docs/adr/

# The engineering log. Tracked briefly on 16 Aug 2026 and untracked again the
# same day, by decision: it is the working record behind the backlog, and it
# belongs with Plans/ below rather than in the published tree. Nothing depends
# on it — `scripts/check_control_chars.py` names it but skips a missing path,
# which is the behaviour it was written for. The code comments that used to cite
# "TASKS.md 5.9" now cite "backlog 5.9": the IDs are stable and worth keeping as
# provenance, but a filename promises a file. CONTRIBUTING.md says once what the
# namespace is. The ADRs keep their prose references — they are dated records of
# what was believed at the time, and rewriting them would defeat the point.
TASKS.md

# ====================
# Planning & Analysis (Internal)
# ====================
# Working notes and audit reports behind the backlog. These stay local: they are
# raw findings, superseded drafts and half-formed conclusions, and TASKS.md —
# now tracked — is where anything from them that held up was written down.
Plans/

# ====================
# Merged into requirements.txt (kept locally, no longer published)
# ====================
# The dependency list was three files chained with `-r`. It is now one file with
# three labelled sections — runtime, training, development — carrying all 33
# packages at identical pins, verified package-by-package against the union of
# the three before this was committed.
#
# The split had a real justification: the training stack (xgboost, imbalanced-
# learn, matplotlib, seaborn) is not reachable from the API, so a deployment
# could skip several hundred megabytes. That is now a comment marking the
# section rather than a separate file, which is the trade made for one obvious
# install command. `pyproject.toml` stays tracked — without it `ruff check`
# goes from clean to 431 errors and CI fails.
requirements-dev.txt
requirements-ml.txt

# ====================
# Superseded artifacts (kept locally, no longer published)
# ====================
# Untracked 16 Aug 2026 with `git rm --cached`, so every one of these is still
# on disk here — only the repository stops carrying them.
#
# The previous job corpus, replaced by data/json/jobs.json. It was 12.25 MB of
# a 16 MB repository — three quarters of everything tracked — and the only
# thing in the codebase that mentioned it was the comment in load_jobs()
# explaining that nothing produces it any more.
data/archive/

# Two experiment directories whose three PNGs each are byte-identical to the
# three in experiment_20260129_195147 (verified by sha256). That directory is
# kept, because it carries the metadata and training summary the plots belong
# to; these two were re-runs that wrote the same pictures again.
models/experiments/experiment_20260129_193509/
models/experiments/experiment_20260129_195005/

# A third way to start the API, referenced by nothing — not the README, not
# run.ps1, not CI. It also hardcoded 0.0.0.0:8000, ignoring API_HOST/API_PORT,
# so it disagreed with both of the other two entrypoints, and it was the only
# file in the repository failing ruff (E402) while sitting outside the scope CI
# lints. `.\run.ps1`, or `python -m uvicorn src.api:app`, both documented in the
# README, are the supported ways in.
run_api.py

